      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "gcc/testsuite     3235k   The tests\ngcc/config        1558k   Every target\ngcc/*             1398k   The middle end and the driver, loose in the directory with no subdirectory\ngcc/cp             316k   The C++ front end\ngcc/fortran        256k   The Fortran front end\ngcc/m2             226k   The Modula-2 front end, mostly written in Modula-2 and not counted here\ngcc/rust           202k   The Rust front end, the newest one in the tree\ngcc/go             101k   The Go front end\ngcc/analyzer        84k   The static analyzer behind -fanalyzer\ngcc/cobol           73k   The COBOL front end, added in GCC 15\ngcc/c               71k   The C front end proper, mostly one very large parser\ngcc/ada             63k   The Ada front end\ngcc/c-family        59k   The parts of C the C and C++ front ends share, including the warnings\ngcc/algol68         43k   The Algol 68 front end, added in GCC 16\ngcc/d               36k   The D front end\ngcc/diagnostics     33k   How an error message gets printed, including the SARIF output\ngcc/jit             33k   libgccjit, which lets a program build code with GCC at run time\ngcc/objc            23k   The Objective C front end, on top of the C one\ngcc/common          12k   Per target bits the driver needs before it knows what it is compiling\ngcc/lto              9k   Link time optimization: reading and writing the on disk representation\ngcc/rtl-ssa          9k   SSA over RTL, which is newer than you think and used by few passes\ngcc/text-art         6k   Drawing diagrams in a terminal, for the analyzer's output\ngcc/sym-exec         4k   A small symbolic execution helper used by one optimization pass\ngcc/ginclude         2k   The headers GCC installs itself, like stddef.h and stdarg.h\n\nand 5 more under two thousand lines, in the notebook",
      "originalText": "gcc/testsuite     3235k   The tests\ngcc/config        1558k   Every target\ngcc/*             1398k   The middle end and the driver, loose in the directory with no subdirectory\ngcc/cp             316k   The C++ front end\ngcc/fortran        256k   The Fortran front end\ngcc/m2             226k   The Modula-2 front end, mostly written in Modula-2 and not counted here\ngcc/rust           202k   The Rust front end, the newest one in the tree\ngcc/go             101k   The Go front end\ngcc/analyzer        84k   The static analyzer behind -fanalyzer\ngcc/cobol           73k   The COBOL front end, added in GCC 15\ngcc/c               71k   The C front end proper, mostly one very large parser\ngcc/ada             63k   The Ada front end\ngcc/c-family        59k   The parts of C the C and C++ front ends share, including the warnings\ngcc/algol68         43k   The Algol 68 front end, added in GCC 16\ngcc/d               36k   The D front end\ngcc/diagnostics     33k   How an error message gets printed, including the SARIF output\ngcc/jit             33k   libgccjit, which lets a program build code with GCC at run time\ngcc/objc            23k   The Objective C front end, on top of the C one\ngcc/common          12k   Per target bits the driver needs before it knows what it is compiling\ngcc/lto              9k   Link time optimization: reading and writing the on disk representation\ngcc/rtl-ssa          9k   SSA over RTL, which is newer than you think and used by few passes\ngcc/text-art         6k   Drawing diagrams in a terminal, for the analyzer's output\ngcc/sym-exec         4k   A small symbolic execution helper used by one optimization pass\ngcc/ginclude         2k   The headers GCC installs itself, like stddef.h and stdarg.h\n\nand 5 more under two thousand lines, in the notebook",
      "fontSize": 11,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "box007",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
